Changelog: 24-10-2026 22:59:30

Added. The owner's remarks on the rebuilt window (24-10-2026). The pills in the owner's order: shadPS4 Install and
Uninstall, Modules Install, Games Install (Extract PKG, which was Games Extract PKG) and Games Add folder, shadNet
Account. The system modules line is Sys modules, Ok in bold green or Missing sys modules in bold red, the count,
the folder and what is missing in its tooltip (its link to the folder went). The shadNet line is the nickname that
signs in alone, Off without one, — before shadPS4 has run, the rest in its tooltip.

Fixed. A click on a link in a state line (a game folder's name) did nothing: the lines allowed text selection only,
not links. Test: a real mouse click on a folder's name asks to take it out.

Changelog: 24-10-2026 22:18:32

Breaking. The window rebuilt on PCSX2 Manager's and RPCS3 Manager's (owner, 24-10-2026: PCSX2 Manager is the
pattern for the other managers). The Play button went: a game starts from Steam. The nightly channel went, as it
went in PCSX2 Manager: the app installs the shadPS4 release it was tried with (an installed nightly build shows as
another version, which Install replaces). Update Game Mode is Update Steam, Covers… is Steam artwork…, the Manual
link is Wiki, and the table's columns are In Steam, Game title, Id, Version and Folder (the folder's name, the path
in its tooltip).

Added. The header's pills spread over the width: Refresh, shadPS4 version, Your games, Available in Steam and Play
time, the time spent in all games as shadPS4 counts it in play_time.txt (per game, with the last start, in the
tooltip; the System modules box went, its line says it). The states beside the title end at the last pill's middle:
the app's, shadNet's and the controller's (looked at every 3 s; a game started from Steam reads the controller there
when it starts). The four numbered steps are six pills: shadPS4 Install and Uninstall, Modules Install (the .sprx
files of a chosen folder copied into shadPS4's module folder, as the owner asked of PCSX2 Manager's BIOS step),
Games Add folder and Extract PKG, shadNet Account. The state lines are short, with more in their tooltips: the
version alone, the modules as a count with a link that opens the folder, the game folders by name, each a link that
takes the folder out of shadPS4's game folders after a question (config.json's install_dirs, as shadPS4's own
Remove Folder does; not while shadPS4 runs). Three tabs the pills' size: Your games, Settings and Log. The
Settings tab holds the settings shadPS4 0.20.0's own window offers for every game (VSync, FSR and its RCAS
sharpening, HDR, the frame rate counter, the sound output and volume, motion controls, the mouse pointer, the
system language, trophy messages, the splash screen), each one key of config.json written the moment it is
changed, the rest of the file kept, never while shadPS4 runs, with Bazzite's volume for shadPS4 beside its volume
(core's sound: on the board shadPS4 is muted there). The Log tab shows the app's log (core's applog), and the run
wrapper writes each game started into it, by its folder's name, with whether a controller was connected; a game
Steam starts without one also gets a desktop notification. The quit hotkeys the app adds are logged. The flat
choice boxes with the thin chevron, and the Steam link under the table, as in the other managers. shadPS4
settings stays under the games, for what the Settings tab does not set (the controller's buttons, a game's own
settings). Tests: the window's layout, the pills and the states, the modules copied, a game folder taken out, the
Settings tab against config.json, Bazzite's volume, the play time from the board's play_time.txt, the controller
state, the log, the run wrapper's log line, and the installer test.

