Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:07:44

Added. Covers from SteamGridDB for the portrait in Steam's library (owner, 22-10-2026), with core's covers. A PS4
game has no 2:3 picture of its own, so the portrait was always drawn from its icon and title. With the suite's
SteamGridDB API key, entered under the new Covers… button (one key for every manager), Update Game Mode first looks
each ticked game up by its title and takes the highest-scored portrait; the wide picture, the banner and the logo stay
the game's own. What is found is kept in ~/.local/share/bc250-shadps4-manager/covers under the game's title ID, so a
game is asked for once; a game in Steam not yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network stops
the lookup with a message and the drawn portrait is used; the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key
nothing changes. The artwork is now drawn in the background job, after the lookup. Test: the cover on the portrait
only, and Covers… with Update Game Mode in the window, with SteamGridDB's answers recorded.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 12:55:41

Release 0.7.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 11:59:11

Added. Extract PKG: an update (CATEGORY gp) for a game in the output folder goes into TITLE_ID-UPDATE beside the
game, which shadPS4 lays over the game when it starts; the game's folder stays as it was. Before, the window
refused, as the game's TITLE_ID folder was not empty, and an update had to be extracted elsewhere and its files
moved over the game by hand. An update already there is replaced when the user says so: the new one is extracted
into a folder beside it and takes its place only when every file was written, else the old one stays. A gp package
without its game in the output folder goes into TITLE_ID as before, as a game with its update in it says gp too. The
command-line tool is unchanged. Test: an update without its game, beside its game, a second one refused and
replaced, and one that fails to extract.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 11:48:18

Added. shadPS4's quit window from a controller and from any keyboard: the app adds to shadPS4's
input_config/global.ini, when it starts, the lines it lacks of Share + Options (Back + Start on every controller),
Ctrl+Shift+End and Ctrl+Shift+End on the keypad. shadPS4 opened it only on Ctrl+Shift+End with the End key of its
own, which a keyboard without one does not have, and from no controller button; a game started from Big Picture on
the desktop could only be quit through Steam. shadPS4's own default goes in too, as shadPS4 adds it only to a file
without hotkey_quit. Tested on the owner's board with a DualSense Edge and a keyboard whose End is on the keypad.
Test: the file made from nothing, and as shadPS4 0.20.0 writes it.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 11:00:15

